# WP-207 §D: under --gc-sections an unchanged file's section dies (its only
# caller in a changed file stops calling it), revives, dies again.
proves: the revival of hop 2 left u.o's SECTIONS, HOLES and .symtab rows true, so the second death is a clean hole
source: WP-207 §D, the two- and three-hop series
edit: c.cc
link: main.o c.o u.o
cflags: -ffunction-sections
options: --gc-sections
expect-full: update-not-implemented (layout|symtab|scan|eh|image): every hop flips a section's liveness, which changes the stored placement (SECTIONS.bits, META.live_hash); `live` is judged against the front's mark and the image takes a new placement only from M2b-3 on (WP-225 gc-lift), so no hop expects a gc UPDATE: a hop that updates fails, a hop that falls back earlier (no-state, small-output) is n/a WP-225 M2b-4: a drawn-in file's layout inputs are produced (fresh ids), and the hop then falls back by a later producer's name: the materializer's `(symtab)` (a drawn-in file's local span or `.symtab` size changes: no symtab plan is wired), the scan's `(scan)` (F-1: a key the drawn-in file defines has a new RESOLVED row, its section the fresh id), or `layout_in`'s `(layout)` (a merge section marked in part). WP-225 M2b-5: with F-1 and the `.symtab` spans lifted the hop reaches front 2 and falls back by its name: front 2's S-47 check `(eh)` (a drawn-in file's `.eh_frame` range at another capacity than the image's) or the capture's `REGIONS` producer `(image)` (P3-3: a Fill hole that is no region's slack).
compilers: gcc kiln
also-reversed: the first link never places u_helper (WP-207 §D: "also with the first link never placing it")
